1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,672
Why does Afghanistan have this strange, long tail?

2
00:00:04,222 --> 00:00:10,914
It's called the Wakhan Corridor. A thin strip of land, about 350 kilometers long.

3
00:00:11,464 --> 00:00:18,516
To its north is Tajikistan. To the south, Pakistan. And at the very end, China.

4
00:00:19,066 --> 00:00:26,790
At one point, it's only 13 kilometers wide. Just a thin line of Afghanistan between Pakistan and Tajikistan.

5
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:35,664
The reason? The Great Game. In the 1800s, British India and the Russian Empire were expanding toward each other.

6
00:00:36,214 --> 00:00:43,194
So in 1893 and 1895, treaties left this strip to Afghanistan, so the two empires would never touch.

7
00:00:43,744 --> 00:00:52,116
Its far end meets China. A border just 92 kilometers long, with the Wakhjir Pass nearly 4,900 meters high.

8
00:00:52,666 --> 00:01:01,494
Today, only about 18,000 people live here. A border drawn by two empires' fear. Follow for more map secrets!
